{
  "valuation_insights": "Costco Wholesale Corporation reported total revenue for fiscal year ended August 30, 2026, of $303.154 billion [C:r1], representing a year-over-year growth of 10.1% [C:g1]. Operating income was $11.685 billion [C:oi1], yielding an operating margin of approximately 3.85% [C:om1]. Net income attributable to the company was $9.226 billion [C:ni1]. GAAP diluted earnings per share (EPS) amounted to $20.76 [C:eps1]. Return on average equity (ROE) reached 28.4% [C:roe1]. Total debt, including current portion, sums to $6.163 billion against equity of $35.803 billion, giving a debt-to-equity ratio of 0.172 [C:debt1]. Free cash flow (operating cash flow minus capital expenditures) stood at $9.382 billion [C:fcf1]. Latest quarterly revenue data and GAAP diluted EPS for the quarter are Not established from the given release lines and exhibits. Based on the closing price of $904.70 on 2026-09-23, the price-to-earnings (P/E) ratio is 43.58 [C:pe1]. \n\nPeer operating margins on a consistent total revenue definition for the comparable fiscal periods are: Walmart Inc. at 4.18% [C:wmtoi], Target Corp. at 4.88% [C:tgtom], and BJ's Wholesale Club Holdings, Inc. at 3.81% [C:bjom]. The margin comparison shows Costco’s margin is below Walmart and Target but slightly above BJ's.\n\nSources follow strict GAAP and XBRL tagging to ensure comparability. The revenue figure is from the tag RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax which is explicitly identified as total revenue, not net sales.\n\n",
